    "summary_one_sentence": "When a team of Miami narcotics detectives uncovers millions in hidden cartel cash inside a dilapidated stash house, paranoia and shifting loyalties threaten to tear them apart from within.",
    "summary_short": "Following a tip off after a colleague's tragic murder, a tactical squad of Miami police officers raids a seemingly ordinary suburban stash house expecting a modest bust. Instead, they discover over twenty million dollars in cash concealed within the attic walls, placing them in immediate, deadly jeopardy. As word of the massive seizure begins to leak, the team must process the crime scene under intense pressure while battling internal corruption, greed, and ruthless external threats. Trapped in a high-stakes standoff, the officers are forced to question where their loyalties truly lie and who among them can still be trusted.",
    "summary_long": "In the wake of the tragic murder of a fellow officer, Miami police officers Lt. Dane Dumars and Det. Sgt. JD Byrne lead their specialized narcotics unit on a sudden raid based on a tip. Expecting to find a modest drug operation, the team arrives at a run-down stash house occupied only by a young resident named Desi. Upon searching the premises, the officers stumble upon a secret compartment holding over $20 million in wrapped cartel cash. Realizing the astronomical value of the seizure, the squad is immediately plunged into a nerve-wracking situation where any misstep could prove fatal. Tension steadily mounts as the team is forced to meticulously process and document the money on-site to satisfy strict internal protocols. As news of the massive cash discovery leaks beyond the house, external threats begin closing in, and paranoia rapidly spreads among the officers. Suspicions arise that someone within the unit or department may be conspiring to keep the fortune for themselves. Surrounded by danger and tempted by life-changing wealth, Dumars and Byrne must navigate a deadly maze of police politics, cartel retaliation, and personal betrayal. Ultimately, the officers are forced into a violent confrontation where survival depends on identifying true allies before time runs out.",
    "synopsis": "Directed by Joe Carnahan and starring Matt Damon and Ben Affleck, 'The Rip' is a gritty crime thriller loosely inspired by a real-life Miami drug raid. The story follows a squad of Miami narcotics detectives who respond to a routine tip, only to stumble upon a concealed stash of over $20 million inside a dilapidated home. As the officers attempt to secure the crime scene and properly count the enormous seizure under strict police protocols, the vast sum of money creates an atmosphere of deep paranoia and mistrust. With dangerous forces closing in and suspicion falling on everyone present, the line between law enforcement and self-preservation blurs, pushing the team to its absolute limit.",
